 "problems": [
  "Scramble-era colony dossiers (niger-coast-protectorate, lagos-colony, royal-niger-company, sierra-leone-colony-and-protectorate, and Gyaman's French protectorate 1888-1897) overlap Cliopatria's aggregate french-africa and british-africa / british-colonial-empire rows and the british-gold-coast row (1873-1960); the renderers must decide which wins, and the af-08 owners of those rows should read this batch's notes.",
  "Counterpart slugs in other groups' dossiers to align: dutch-gold-coast uses swedish-empire and brandenburg-prussia (this batch has swedish-gold-coast and brandenburger-gold-coast); freetown-colony names british-colonial-empire as its successor (sierra-leone-colony-and-protectorate now exists); akwamu's 1730 loss names 'Akyem and their allies' (akyem-abuakwa now exists); ashanti-empire uses strings 'Gyaman', 'Wassa', 'Akyem (Abuakwa, Kotoku)'; oyo-empire names new-oyo, which has no dossier.",
  "Date disagreements between this batch and others are recorded in the dossier notes: Gyaman (page: Asante defeat 1740-41, occupation 1819-1874; ashanti-empire dossier: 1732 and vassal until 1895); Dahomey tribute to Oyo (1730 / 1732 / 1748 to 1823 / 1827 / 1832); Bono's fall (1722 vs 1723); Egba end (1914 vs 1918); Fante page says the Dutch sold in 1870 (1872 elsewhere).",
  "Pages that did not load: Nyanaoase, Ijebu Expedition, Kingdom of Porto-Novo, Kingdom of Lagos, Kingdom of Ketu, Anlo Kingdom, Owu War (the first three and Lagos were replaced by sibling pages; Ketu, Anlo and Owu War were not).",
  "Nearly every shape is a stand-in (a named region or a circle round named towns); no page gives a frontier. Only Dahomey, Ife and Egba use an infobox area. All certainty entries are soft. Capital coordinates for Akyem Abuakwa (Kyebi) and Gyaman (Amanvi, at the Bondoukou point) are approximate.",
  "Cliopatria's british-gold-coast row starts in 1873, a year before the colony's establishment (24 July 1874); Fante Confederacy (to 1873) and Akyem Abuakwa (to 1852) hand to it or to british-colonial-empire, and the British forts of 1821-1873 have no dossier.",
  "The Oba of Lagos page gives a reign list with gaps, the Kalabari page a ruler table with approximate dates: neither was entered as identity.rulers."
 ]
}